import{_ as t,o,c as a,a2 as s}from"./chunks/framework.BN3Eol-0.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"ADR-096 — Indexable entity pages and the SEO surface","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"adr/ADR-096.md","filePath":"adr/ADR-096.md"}'),n={name:"adr/ADR-096.md"};function i(r,e,d,c,l,h){return o(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[s('<h1 id="adr-096-—-indexable-entity-pages-and-the-seo-surface" tabindex="-1">ADR-096 — Indexable entity pages and the SEO surface <a class="header-anchor" href="#adr-096-—-indexable-entity-pages-and-the-seo-surface" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;ADR-096 — Indexable entity pages and the SEO surface&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Status · Accepted · 2026-11-09 (operator; amended with decisions 8–12) · 0.9.8 plan item 0 (operator, 2026-11-08) · evidence in <code>docs/wip/2026-11-08-seo-review/</code> · builds on <strong>ADR-034</strong> (prerender, server-only loads) and the <code>#519</code> hreflang work · the <code>/c/*</code> share stubs of the collectible cards stay as they are</p></blockquote><h2 id="context" tabindex="-1">Context <a class="header-anchor" href="#context" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Context&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The 2026-11-08 SEO audit of the build found that search engines could rank almost none of what Orrery knows. Every mission, vehicle, landing site, body and Lab calculator lived only in a client-side panel (<code>/missions?id=</code>, <code>/fleet?id=</code>, <code>/moon?site=</code>, <code>/explore?id=</code>, the <code>/lab</code> picker); those URLs canonicalise to their hub, so the entity text never reached prerendered HTML. The only per-entity pages were the 523 <code>/c/*</code> card stubs — en-US, noindex, redirecting. Around that: no Open Graph or JSON-LD on any page, 476 pages without a description, 42 titled just &quot;Orrery&quot;, a 7 MB single-file sitemap, and the GitHub Pages staging mirror outranking the real site for &quot;porkchop plot calculator&quot; despite its canonical tags.</p><h2 id="decision" tabindex="-1">Decision <a class="header-anchor" href="#decision" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Decision&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>One indexable page per entity, in every locale,</strong> prerendered from the data and overlays the panels already use — no new text, the panels&#39; own label messages: <code>/missions/&lt;id&gt;</code> (126), <code>/fleet/&lt;id&gt;</code> (294), <code>/moon|mars|venus/&lt;site&gt;</code> (58), <code>/explore/&lt;body&gt;</code> (48: planets, moons, small bodies), <code>/lab/&lt;formula&gt;</code> (65). × 14 locales = 8,302 pages. Each has H1, facts, the long text, links between entities (mission ↔ vehicle ↔ site), and an &quot;Open in Orrery&quot; link to the in-app view. The in-app panels stay the app; the pages are what search engines and shared links land on.</li><li><strong>Server-only loads</strong> (<code>+page.server.ts</code>) for every entity route: the JSON they read stays out of client JS (a universal load put <code>/fleet/[id]</code> at 51 KB against its 30 KB route budget), and loaders take the prerender <code>fetch</code> (<code>getFleet</code>, <code>getSiteStory</code>, new <code>getSiteEntity</code>, <code>getBodyEntity</code>). The Lab formula ids are mirrored in <code>static/data/lab-formulas.json</code> because <code>scripts/site-routes.mjs</code> (plain Node) cannot import the TS registry; a test pins it to <code>REGISTRY</code>.</li><li><strong>One route list</strong> — <code>scripts/site-routes.mjs</code> seeds the per-locale prerender and the sitemaps, so neither can drift. Sitemaps: <code>/sitemap.xml</code> is an index of 14 <code>/sitemaps/&lt;locale&gt;.xml</code>. No <code>&lt;lastmod&gt;</code>: CI builds from a depth-1 checkout without <code>.git</code> in the Docker context, so dates would all be the build commit&#39;s.</li><li><strong>Head tags from one place each.</strong> <code>metaDescription()</code> (≤160, sentence cut) and <code>pageTitle()</code> (≤60, &quot;Topic — subtitle&quot; keeps the topic) in <code>$lib/seo</code>; Open Graph + Twitter tags are added to every page by <code>addSocialMeta()</code> in the prerender hook from the page&#39;s own title, description and canonical (a page&#39;s own <code>og:image</code> — mission / fleet cards — wins); JSON-LD via <code>&lt;JsonLd&gt;</code> (<code>Article</code> + <code>BreadcrumbList</code> on reading and entity pages, <code>WebSite</code> + <code>Organization</code> on home).</li><li><strong>The staging mirror is noindex</strong> (any build with a base path): no canonical, no hreflang.</li><li><strong>The gate.</strong> <code>scripts/check-seo.mjs</code> runs in every <code>npm run build</code>: per indexable page one title (not the bare brand, ≤90), one description (≤160), self canonical, complete hreflang with built targets, og/twitter tags, JSON-LD that parses, one H1, no noindex; sitemaps = indexable pages; on the mirror, every page noindex.</li><li><strong>Mobile ships none of it.</strong> <code>prune-streamed-assets.mjs</code> drops the entity pages and their <code>__data.json</code>, the sitemaps and the stubs (mobile build 75.6 MB of its 77 MB budget).</li></ol><p>Amended 2026-11-09 with the operator&#39;s decisions on the open questions:</p><ol start="8"><li><strong>Hub links in the footer.</strong> Explore · Worlds · Catalog · Learn on every page, with the nav&#39;s own labels: the four hub pages were linked only from TV mode and the sitemap.</li><li><strong>HTML stays uncached at the edge.</strong> Cloudflare caches <code>/_app/immutable</code> only; caching HTML would need a purge on every deploy, or cached pages point at deleted chunks. Revisit if Search Console shows slow time to first byte.</li><li><strong>Search titles beside poetic headings.</strong> Essays, programs, science sections and weak science articles carry <code>seo_title</code> / <code>seo_description</code> in their overlays (14 locales); <code>&lt;title&gt;</code>, og and the meta description use them, the visible H1 and JSON-LD keep the poetic title.</li><li><strong>A–Z index on the hubs.</strong> <code>/missions</code>, <code>/fleet</code>, <code>/moon</code>, <code>/mars</code>, <code>/venus</code> and <code>/explore</code> prerender a collapsed list linking every entity page (server load, no client JS cost): panels open on a click, which crawlers don&#39;t make.</li><li><strong>Thin-page regression floor.</strong> All entity pages stay indexable; thin ones are enriched from localized data the panels already show or the data files hold (linked missions with their one-liners, sites, crew, museums, related hardware, orbit and size figures, science sections, a lab formula&#39;s dials, defaults, worked result and assumptions) — no new prose. <code>check-seo.mjs</code> then fails an entity page whose <code>&lt;main&gt;</code> text is under its locale&#39;s character floor (<code>THIN_MIN_CHARS</code>). Characters, not words, because words are not a unit that holds across languages; per locale because the same content is ~1.1-1.2x the English length in the Latin / Cyrillic locales, ~1.0x in hi / ar and ~0.55-0.6x in zh-CN / ja / ko. Each floor is 95 % of that locale&#39;s thinnest page after the enrichment (en-US 350, zh-CN 175), so it guards against regressions rather than judging content; <code>CHECK_SEO_FLOORS=1 node scripts/check-seo.mjs</code> re-measures it.</li></ol><h2 id="consequences" tabindex="-1">Consequences <a class="header-anchor" href="#consequences" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Consequences&quot;">​</a></h2><p><strong>Positive.</strong> 12,166 indexable pages (was 3,892), each with its own text, title, description, share card and structured data; every entity reachable by a stable URL in its reader&#39;s language; regressions fail the build instead of surfacing in Search Console weeks later.</p><p><strong>Negative.</strong> The web build grows by ~212 MB of HTML + <code>__data.json</code> and the prerender by a few minutes; the staging (GitHub Pages) publish carries it too. Some entity pages stay short where the data is thin; after the enrichment the shortest is 369 characters in en-US (<code>lab/weight</code>) and 27 of 8,303 were still under the old 80-word floor (mostly ko / sr-Cyrl, whose words are shorter or longer than English ones). Two views of every entity now exist; a change to what a panel shows should be mirrored on its page.</p><p><strong>Neutral.</strong> The panels do not link to the pages (decision 11 links them from the hubs instead); program rosters keep their <code>?id=</code> links into the 3D views.</p><h2 id="alternatives-considered" tabindex="-1">Alternatives considered <a class="header-anchor" href="#alternatives-considered" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Alternatives considered&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Make the <code>/c/*</code> stubs indexable.</strong> They redirect humans away instantly (Google treats that as a doorway / soft 404) and are en-US only. Rejected.</li><li><strong>Render the panels server-side on the hub routes</strong> (<code>/missions?id=</code> as one URL per entity). Query-string variants of one route are weak canonicals, and the hubs are 3D / client-heavy pages. Rejected.</li><li><strong>Hand-written SEO copy per entity.</strong> ~8,000 pages × 14 locales of new prose is a translation programme, not a change; the existing overlays already carry the text. Deferred: per-page SEO titles beside the poetic H1s of essays / programs / science need the operator&#39;s per-page yes.</li><li><strong>A dedicated JS route list for Lab formulas generated at build.</strong> A new build step for 65 ids; the guarded JSON file is smaller and fails loudly when it drifts.</li></ul>',14)])])}const u=t(n,[["render",i]]);export{g as __pageData,u as default};
